# Monorepo Architecture Rule

- Keep dependency direction stable: `apps -> internal(runtime) -> domains(api/contracts)`.
- Runtime (`internal`) is the only state center.
- Domains are stateless plugins.
- Apps are entry layers only.
- Cross-module communication must go through Event contracts.
- Do not bypass runtime with direct domain-to-domain calls.

## Layer constraints

- `apps/*`:
  - allowed: transport adapters, auth/parsing, invoke runtime, response rendering.
  - forbidden: domain business orchestration, direct vendor SDK/database business ops.
- Gateway HTTP/WS path conventions: see `12-http-routing` (default `/api` without version; domain evolution via event contracts, not URL major versions).
- `internal/*`:
  - allowed: session, event dispatcher, snapshot/replay, sequencer, ws protocol.
  - forbidden: UI/business page logic, depending on `apps` implementations.
- `domains/*`:
  - allowed: business logic via event input/output contracts.
  - forbidden: websocket/session store/redis/kafka wiring, runtime impl dependency.
- `pkg|packages/*`:
  - allowed: infrastructure adapters.
  - forbidden: business logic and runtime/domain coupling.

